  "note": "UX-420: one CI run's per-file totals, so a later CI run can be read against CI rather than against the floors in tests/tiers.py, which describe a developer machine. Refresh from a CI run's ci-reference-candidate artifact, or the log of its tier-reference job, which is this same tool's --record taken on the runner whose clock this document is in - not from a local --record (UX-418, UX-447). UX-457: this document is a whole re-record, taken from run 33413312096's tier-reference job (head c41a27e) rather than appended to; the six hand-appends recorded in rounds 67-71 are retired with it. One append since, on the same terms as those six: test_a_candidate_is_confirmed_alone.py landed after that record and run 33422781976's gate named it at 2.3s with the run at x0.99 shift, so 2.32 = 2.3 / 0.99. Two more appends on the same terms, from run 33493747354's tier-reference job (head 66a3274, shift x1.006): test_the_trace_census_reads_both_ends.py 6.76 and test_a_generated_project_builds.py 0.17. The gate named only the first - the second is bst-gated and its clauses skip in the `test` job, so it costs 0.17s there and never reached CI_DRIFT_SECONDS. Round 72 again, from run 33495069593's tier-reference job (head ca22e60): test_emphasis_is_a_budget.py 12.6 -> 16.86 and test_the_shape_conclusions_have_a_negative_case.py 0.07. The first is NOT a file this branch touched: its raw seconds read 12.58 in the recording run, 22.5 in run 33493747354 and 16.86 here, so 16.86 is the middle of the three and is the value that run's own candidate carries. See UX-476, which is about a file nobody touched crossing both gates on two consecutive runs, and why a wholesale re-record is deferred to that row rather than done here. Round 73, from run 33505406758's gate (test (3.11), shift x0.91): test_every_finding_reaches_a_fixture.py 1.76 = 1.6 / 0.91, a file this round added;. test_the_page_has_a_reader.py was raised 8.8 -> 15.05 in the same commit and then PUT BACK: run 33508941693, the